# djot.v

A [djot](https://djot.net) parser written and verified in
[Rocq](https://rocq-prover.org), and extracted to OCaml.

djot was designed around a few goals: parsing never backtracks, text means
the same thing inside a container as outside it, a link is recognized
without looking at the rest of the document, and a paragraph can be
hard-wrapped anywhere. Here those goals are theorems about the parser.

djot is one setting of the parser. Its inline delimiters can be respelled,
its constructs can be switched off, and extensions can be switched on. For
each setting, the proofs say which of the properties it keeps. A
Markdown-like profile, for example, keeps no backtracking and uniformity,
and gives up safe hard-wrapping.

- [Playground](playground/): run the parser in the browser, change the
  profile, and see which properties the profile keeps.
- [Extensions](extensions/): the syntax of each extension.
- [OCaml API](api/): the extracted parser as a library.

